WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:03.943
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.985 --> 00:07.048
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.090 --> 00:10.785
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.827 --> 00:13.788
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.830 --> 00:17.158
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.200 --> 00:20.528
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.570 --> 00:21.963
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.005 --> 00:23.664
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.706 --> 00:28.927
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.302 --> 00:36.510
<i>Is Netflix Streaming</i>

00:36.552 --> 00:38.079
<i>the right choice for you?</i>

00:38.121 --> 00:39.814
<i>Well, if you like movies in HD,</i>

00:39.856 --> 00:42.016
<i>then frozen pixels, then HD again,</i>

00:42.058 --> 00:43.918
<i>the answer is "yes."</i>

00:43.960 --> 00:47.788
<i>And if you love the golden
year of movies, 2003,</i>

00:47.830 --> 00:49.690
<i>then we might have some of
what you're looking for.</i>

00:49.732 --> 00:51.726
<i>Netflix Streaming:
buffer for 20 minutes,</i>

00:51.768 --> 00:55.553
<i>then watch 35 minutes of a
movie with Jason Statham.</i>

00:55.904 --> 00:57.543
Oh, look what came,

00:57.585 --> 00:59.712
the free DVD from my PBS pledge.

00:59.754 --> 01:01.567
Whatever it is, we're not watching it.

01:01.609 --> 01:02.752
Peter, trust me,

01:02.794 --> 01:05.155
you of all people could really
learn something from this.

01:05.197 --> 01:07.724
It's a documentary about
the food industry called,

01:07.766 --> 01:09.259
<i>Food Kills.</i>

01:09.301 --> 01:11.561
<i>Huh. Says here that
Colon Health Magazine</i>

01:11.603 --> 01:12.953
gave it two thumbs in.

01:20.963 --> 01:23.573
Hi, I'm Matt Lauer's
cousin, Stephen McCormick.

01:23.615 --> 01:25.241
Our moms are sisters.

01:25.283 --> 01:27.777
America is gorging itself
on processed food,

01:27.819 --> 01:29.612
creating an obesity epidemic.

01:29.654 --> 01:31.281
We've abandoned natural foods

01:31.323 --> 01:33.783
for chemicals, additives
and refined sugars.

01:33.825 --> 01:37.020
At this rate, this is what
the future will look like.

01:37.062 --> 01:38.722
<i>Those are flying cars,</i>

01:38.764 --> 01:40.924
<i>but the people in them are too fat.</i>

01:40.966 --> 01:43.793
Oh, no, I left my baby in there.

01:43.835 --> 01:45.695
Without drastic changes in our diet,

01:45.737 --> 01:48.131
Americans are headed for
a health catastrophe.

01:48.173 --> 01:50.200
For more, go to our website at

01:50.242 --> 01:53.103
"double-u double-u
double-u dot PBS dot com."

01:53.145 --> 01:55.405
That's "www" dot,

01:55.447 --> 01:57.273
the word "double-u" three times,

01:57.315 --> 01:59.309
the word "dot," "PBS,"

01:59.351 --> 02:00.910
the word "dot" again,

02:00.952 --> 02:03.146
the word "com," dot com.

02:03.188 --> 02:06.583
There was a miscommunication
when we registered our website.

02:06.625 --> 02:08.218
Well, that's it, from now on,

02:08.260 --> 02:09.919
we're eating healthy around here.

02:09.961 --> 02:11.900
We're gonna feel better and
we're gonna look better.

02:11.942 --> 02:14.557
Well, looking better doesn't
always solve your problems, Lois.

02:14.599 --> 02:17.174
It sure didn't work for Droopy
Dog when he got that facelift.

02:17.216 --> 02:21.297
Contrary to my appearance,
I'm still not happy.

02:21.339 --> 02:26.302
Please study my brain so that
others don't suffer as I have.

02:37.886 --> 02:40.150
Thanks for coming to my
birthday party, you guys.

02:40.192 --> 02:42.352
And Esther, I'm so sorry
you ripped your perineum

02:42.394 --> 02:43.853
